WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.167
-Hi, Jimmy, how are you?

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:03.934
-Thank you for coming on. Thanks for playing the game.

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:06.434
I want to talk about all these -- all this exciting news.

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:07.968
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. There's a lot going on.

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:09.601
-It's -- It's a lot. -Breaking news.

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:11.567
-I mean, you're -- you're acting, but you're also

00:00:11.567 --> 00:00:13.534
producing all these multiple projects.

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:14.701
-Yeah.

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:17.033
-"Russian Doll" season two, it started today.

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:19.701
-Yeah, yeah. It's now streaming. Yeah.

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:21.734
And, uh -- Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.734
So... -You know what, by the way?

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.734
I -- I follow you on the socials.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:27.367
-Oh. -Yeah, because, you know.

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:29.000
Well, you're very funny. -No, no, I'm going to

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.434
follow back eventually.

00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:31.934
-Thank you, yeah, yeah.

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:33.567
I just wanted to put it -- say it out loud on live television.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:34.901
But, you know, I didn't realize --

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.801
you love the game Wordle, by the way.

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:38.067
I don't know if you know this.

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:39.467
-Oh, I do. -You love it.

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:41.100
-I do feel terrible, 'cause I feel like

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.367
these nice people are following,

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:44.000
and they're hoping for something,

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.634
but it's just really my Wordle and Quordle and Octordle

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:53.400
and Sedecordle and Duotrigordle scores.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.767
-Yeah.

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:56.367
-Duotrigordle is a lot of fun you see,

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:59.133
because it's 32 grids at once.

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:02.033
-That's too many for me. -It's just the right amount.

00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:03.234
-It really --

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:04.567
-Really? That's where you want to go?

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:05.767
-Oh, that's that sweet spot, Jimmy.

00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:06.968
-What do you love about it?

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:08.634
"Ooh, that's that sweet spot, Jimmy."

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:11.234
-How do you -- why do you love Wordle game?

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:12.634
Why do you love those --

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:15.100
-Eh, you know, I like to hear the click,

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.834
the white-noise sound, the click.

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:22.033
And when you tap the buttons, you feel like a cat.

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:23.267
It also incorporates...

00:01:23.267 --> 00:01:24.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.634 --> 00:01:27.801
...reading and words, which I like, and tapping.

00:01:27.801 --> 00:01:30.467
And it's not exclusive to that.

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:34.267
I also enjoy chess and the crossword

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:36.000
and the "New York Times" Spelling Bee.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.701
-Wait. -So I have a lot of hobbies.

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:39.968
-Wait. -I do it all on the phone.

00:01:39.968 --> 00:01:42.767
I'm essentially a cyborg, at this point.

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:45.200
And I'm doing, at least,

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.200
I would say four to six hours a day of gaming.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.200
-Oh, wow. Congratulations. Oh, my God.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.734
-Thank you so much.

00:01:50.734 --> 00:01:52.234
-You got to get a Twitch channel next.

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:55.868
-Yeah. And I also -- I beat "Zelda" during the pandemic.

00:01:55.868 --> 00:01:58.133
-Oh, wasn't that unbelievable? -Yeah, I'm getting a lot done.

00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.667
-Look at you! I love this! -Yeah.

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:02.467
And the show is out today. -And there you go, yeah.

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:05.300
And it's out today. -So that's great.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.501
-You know, I've known you for a long time,

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:08.901
love everything you do.

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:10.634
"Orange is the New Black." Congratulations. That was great.

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:13.033
And then you go, "Yeah, I'm gonna come up with this idea

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:15.300
for 'Russian Doll' and produce it with Amy Poehler...

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.000
-Yeah. -...and just figure this out."

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.400
How did you even -- how did you sell the idea of "Russian Doll"?

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.534
-Oh, I'm not sure how we sold it.

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:26.200
I guess the algorithm. Um, but --

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.868
-It's great. You did a fantastic job with it.

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:30.701
-Aw. Thank you so much. We work very hard.

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:33.534
I really hope you guys like it.

00:02:33.534 --> 00:02:35.667
But, well what happened back --

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:38.033
Well, I've known you guys because of Maya --

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:40.534
-Yeah. -You and Amy and Fred

00:02:40.534 --> 00:02:42.801
and everything for like 25 years or something now.

00:02:42.801 --> 00:02:44.200
-Wild.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.367
-And -- And one day Amy called me.

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:48.067
I was at home. I was watching "NYPD Blue."

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.934
I was on a real bender.

00:02:49.934 --> 00:02:53.434
I'm a little bit in love with Dennis Franz as Andy Sipowicz.

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:55.067
-Oh, I remember. -I just think he's a real cutie.

00:02:55.067 --> 00:02:56.534
And, uh --

00:02:56.534 --> 00:02:58.234
So, I was watching that,

00:02:58.234 --> 00:03:00.534
you know, eating ice cream and chicken.

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:05.334
And she calls me up and she says,

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:07.734
"Hey, I just wanted to say, as long as I've known you,

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:10.200
you've always been the oldest girl in the world."

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.734
And I said, "Why are you calling and insulting me?"

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:14.267
-"I don't have time for this. Please."

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:16.133
-"I'm having a tough enough time as it is, Amy."

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:17.901
-"I'm hanging up the phone now. Why would you say that?"

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:19.968
-She said, "I think we should make a show about that."

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:22.300
And so we made that show. "Old Soul."

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.767
It didn't get picked up.

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:25.100
But then we made "Russian Doll."

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.934
And -- Yeah. -Wow.

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:28.834
-And so -- Now streaming, like I said.

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:30.100
-So "Russian Doll" -- And it was --

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:34.200
I loved it. I go, "That was trippy."

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.234
You did -- You just played it so well.

00:03:36.234 --> 00:03:38.534
But it's basically like a "Groundhog Day" type of vibe,

00:03:38.534 --> 00:03:40.033
where you kept dying each episode

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:42.701
and then reliving your -- your birthday.

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:44.467
But what is season two about?

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:47.868
-Yes, well, this year, it's a bit of a deeper dive.

00:03:47.868 --> 00:03:49.934
If you think of the matryoshka doll,

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:52.501
there's, you know, ever deeper dolls inside of there.

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:54.934
And so if season one

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:57.634
was sort of a meditation on "how do I stop dying?",

00:03:57.634 --> 00:04:00.100
in a way, season two is posing the question of,

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.667
"How do I start living?"

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:03.501
So it's -- it kind of gets in --

00:04:03.501 --> 00:04:06.501
It's a real psychedelic, philosophical romp,

00:04:06.501 --> 00:04:09.200
and if that's your scene, you'll really enjoy yourself.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.033
-Yeah. -It's a wild ride.

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:12.901
I cannot believe they let us make it.

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:14.000
-Yeah. -Yeah.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.167
-Yeah, it looks great.

00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:16.501
I know Annie Murphy joined the cast, too.

00:04:16.501 --> 00:04:18.167
-Yeah, Annie Murphy is a sensation.

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:20.467
-She's fantastic. You guys together? Forget it.

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:23.133
-Oh, my God. And she looks like a Scorsese character in this.

00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:25.100
I mean, she is just -- does excellent work.

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:26.901
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:26.901 --> 00:04:30.434
Here is Natasha Lyonne in "Russian Doll," season two.

00:04:30.434 --> 00:04:32.200
-Can I get a bourbon?

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.734
-A bourbon? You sure about that, hon?

00:04:33.734 --> 00:04:36.601
-Yeah, "hon." That's arguably the only thing I'm sure of.

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:39.701
Basic concepts like time and space are suddenly eluding me.

00:04:39.701 --> 00:04:42.601
I mean, last night, this place was mayhem cause Wi-Fi went out,

00:04:42.601 --> 00:04:44.033
but in the new here and now,

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:47.601
apparently gratuitous nudity is back in play.

00:04:47.601 --> 00:04:50.767
Well, my past, your future.

00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:53.467
Begs the question... am I haunting you...

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:55.000
or are you haunting me?

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.701
-You seem pretty relaxed for a ghost.

00:04:57.701 --> 00:04:59.601
-Tell you what I did not expect --

00:04:59.601 --> 00:05:00.734
It's for the 6 train

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:03.234
to run through some kind of a worm hole.

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:04.501
Hit me, please.

00:05:04.501 --> 00:05:06.133
-You're a time traveler.

00:05:06.133 --> 00:05:09.234
-Eh. I prefer the term "time prisoner."

00:05:09.234 --> 00:05:11.534
-Hm. -Yeah, come on.

00:05:11.534 --> 00:05:13.801
Come on, buddy.

00:05:13.801 --> 00:05:16.434
I also want to say,

00:05:16.434 --> 00:05:20.334
you got to -- you got to direct some of these.

00:05:20.334 --> 00:05:22.567
-Oh, yeah, yeah. I direct about half the season.

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:24.234
And, you know, we write it,

00:05:24.234 --> 00:05:26.601
and we've got a pretty sensational thing --

00:05:26.601 --> 00:05:28.334
an all-ladies writers' room.

00:05:28.334 --> 00:05:29.801
They're geniuses. I swear to God.

00:05:29.801 --> 00:05:31.534
-Hey. I'm so happy for you. -Yeah, yeah.

00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:33.067
-Thanks for coming on. It's always so great to see you.

00:05:33.067 --> 00:05:35.501
Natasha Lyonne, everybody. Check out the new season

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:38.801
of "Russian Doll," streaming right now on Netflix.

